cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OASIS: certified spatial association analysis for serial-section single-plex IHC"
message: "If you use OASIS in work you publish, please cite it. Work that uses the segmentation should also cite InstanSeg (see models/NOTICE.md), and work that uses registration certification should also cite LoFTR (see paper.bib)."
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/smukilan9-ship-it/OASIS"
# Bump these together with the release tag, and keep them equal to it. A CITATION.cff whose
# version does not match the tag it ships in sends every citation to the wrong artefact.
version: 0.1.2
date-released: 2026-08-04
abstract: >-
  OASIS quantifies DAB-positive cells in brightfield immunohistochemistry and
  measures population-level spatial association between two markers stained on
  serial sections. Registration between the two sections is certified before any
  statistic is reported: a pair that cannot be aligned to a stated cell-scale
  error is flagged and excluded rather than analysed anyway. The association
  statistic is the cross-type Ripley's K function against a Monte Carlo null
  bounded by the certified analysis window. It is a population statistic and does
  not assert single-cell co-expression, which serial sections cannot establish.
keywords:
  - digital pathology
  - immunohistochemistry
  - image registration
  - spatial statistics
  - Ripley's K
authors:
  # TODO before release: full name as it should appear in a citation, plus ORCID
  # and affiliation. These must match paper.md, which carries the same TODOs.
  # An incorrect ORCID is worse than an absent one, so both are left unset here.
  - given-names: Mukilan
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # affiliation: ""
